 ### [Sparse Latent Space for 4D Novel View Synthesis (SLS4D)](18112-sparse-latent-space-for-4d-novel-view-synthesis-sls4d.md)
-SLS4D is a method for 4D novel-view synthesis that represents dynamic radiance fields using a learnable sparse latent space, reducing network parameters compared to dense grid discretizations while maintaining high-frequency detail via attention-based interpolation [18112-sparse-latent-space-for-4d-novel-view-synthesis-sls4d.md]. It differs from dense grid methods (like TiNeuVox) by avoiding the $O(N^3TF)$ space complexity of 4D grids, and from per-image latent code methods by offering better generalization across time through continuous temporal interpolation.
