 ### [Neural Feature Fusion Fields (N3F)](18114-neural-feature-fusion-fields-n3f.md)
-Neural Feature Fusion Fields (N3F) is a method that distills dense 2D image features from a pre-trained teacher network into a 3D neural field (student) via differentiable volumetric rendering, enabling 3D-aware feature representation [18114-neural-feature-fusion-fields-n3f.md]. Unlike Semantic NeRF or Panoptic NeRF which fuse discrete semantic labels, N3F fuses continuous dense feature vectors, allowing for open-world applications without manual labels. It differs from standard feature distillation because the student operates in 3D world space (ensuring spatial consistency) while the teacher operates in 2D image space.
