 ### [CLNeRF Architecture with Embeddings](18159-clnerf-architecture-with-embeddings.md)
-CLNeRF is a model architecture modification for NeRF that enables continual learning by incorporating scene changes (appearance and geometry) over time within a single model, preventing model size growth as new scans are added [18159-clnerf-architecture-with-embeddings.md]. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like MIMO-DONeRF and SLS4D by using explicit, trainable per-scan embedding vectors rather than latent space compression or multi-instance networks, allowing for efficient updates and low overhead for generative replay.
